{"name":"Smoky Sweet potato and chickpea stew","permalink":"smoky-sweet-potato-chickpea-stew","edit":"https://github.com/The-Silverwood-Institute/Recibase/tree/master/src/main/scala/se/reciba/api/recibase/recipes/SmokyChickpeaStew.scala","source":"https://www.budgetbytes.com/smoky-potato-chickpea-stew/","description":"A simple yet hearty vegan stew","tagline":null,"notes":[],"dated_notes":[],"tags":["Vegan","Scales","Freezes"],"inherited_tags":["Pescatarian","Vegetarian-ish","Vegetarian","Vegan-ish"],"image":null,"ingredients_blocks":[{"name":null,"ingredients":[{"name":"Sweet Potatoes","quantity":"620g","prep":"chopped in 1cm cubes","notes":null},{"name":"Garlic Cloves","quantity":"4","prep":"finely chopped or crushed","notes":null},{"name":"Carrots","quantity":"2","prep":"diced","notes":"optional"},{"name":"Onions","quantity":"2","prep":"chopped","notes":null},{"name":"Red pepper","quantity":"1","prep":"sliced","notes":null},{"name":"Fresh ginger","quantity":"2 tsp","prep":"grated or finely chopped","notes":null},{"name":"Spinach","quantity":"a large handful","prep":"chopped","notes":"alternatively kale"},{"name":"Sundried tomatoes","quantity":"285g","prep":"chopped","notes":null},{"name":"Vegetarian chorizo sausages","quantity":"6","prep":null,"notes":"optional"},{"name":"Kidney Beans","quantity":"1 400g tin","prep":null,"notes":null},{"name":"Chopped tomatoes","quantity":"1 400g tin","prep":null,"notes":null},{"name":"Chickpeas","quantity":"2 400g tins","prep":null,"notes":null},{"name":"Curry powder","quantity":"2 tsps","prep":null,"notes":null},{"name":"Smoked paprika","quantity":"several teaspoons","prep":null,"notes":null},{"name":"Stock cube","quantity":null,"prep":null,"notes":null},{"name":"Olive oil","quantity":null,"prep":null,"notes":null}]}],"method":["If you're adding the veggie chorizo sausages, preheat the oven per packet instructions.","Add some olive oil to a large soup/stew pot.","Add the onion, carrots, garlic and ginger to the pot and saute on a medium heat until soft.","Meanwhile, disolve the stock cube in boiling water and drain the chickpeas.","Add the smoked paprika and curry powder and cook the spices for a minute or two.","Add the potatoes, chickpeas, red pepper, sundried tomatoes and chopped tomatoes.","Turn up the heat to bring to a boil, then turn down to a light simmer for 45m, sturring occasionaly.","Meanwhile, cook the veggie sausages and allow to cool, then slice into 2cm pieces.","Add the sausages and kidney beans then simmer for a further 5-10m","Throw in the spinach shortly before serving"]}